      "created_via": "codex",
      "creative_liberties_note": "“At day's end” supplies a plausible but unstated setting. “I'm ready” shifts the speaker's intention to lie down and sleep into a statement of readiness. “Have put my life back together” introduces prior disruption and completed restoration beyond the Hebrew's assurance of security.",
